# Dashboard guide

The Dashboard is the main place to create, observe, and control agent Sessions. The hosted Remote Dashboard connects securely to agents running on your device.

## Open the Dashboard

Use [app.pontia.dev](https://app.pontia.dev) and select a registered device. See [Remote access](/docs/remote-access) if the device is not registered yet.

### Local Dashboard

The local Dashboard is available at <http://127.0.0.1:8080/dashboard> and uses the `external_api_token` from `$PONTIA_HOME/config.toml`. Access from another device requires a secure tunnel or forwarding setup.

## Activate a Workspace

A Workspace is the project directory in which an agent runs. Before creating a Session, use [Workspaces](https://app.pontia.dev/workspaces) to browse one of the configured roots and activate the project directory.

Activate directories within your configured Workspace Browser roots. The first initialization uses your home directory as the default root. See [Workspaces](/docs/workspaces) to restrict or change the available roots.

## Start a Session

1. Open [New chat](https://app.pontia.dev/).
2. Select an active Workspace.
3. Select an enabled Agent Client, such as Pi, Codex, Claude Code, or Grok Build.
4. For Pi, Codex, or Claude Code, choose a model or keep the client default. For Pi models that support reasoning, you can also choose the reasoning effort.
5. Describe the job and submit the prompt.

Pontia creates a durable Session and starts the selected Agent Client on your device. The Session remains available in Pontia even when you navigate away from the chat.

## Control active work

The chat page streams the conversation and work steps exposed by the Agent Client. While using a Session, you can:

- send another message when the agent is idle;
- queue input while a supported Agent Client is busy;
- interrupt the current Turn when the Client supports interruption;
- answer tool and permission requests, such as command approvals, when the Client asks for them;
- retry or dismiss Inbox messages whose delivery failed;
- type `@` to find files and directories in the active Workspace;
- attach files with the **+** button in the composer, up to 1 GiB each;
- edit an eligible earlier user message to branch from that point in the native conversation history.

The Inbox tracks submitted messages waiting for delivery or queued by an Agent Client.

## Files in replies

An agent shows you a file by writing its absolute path in a reply. A Markdown link such as `[report](/work/report.pdf)` appears in the text; click it to preview or download the file. To attach files, the agent writes an attachments block, a code block with the language `attachments` and one absolute path per line:

```attachments
/work/report.pdf
/work/chart.png
```

The files appear as one card below the reply, where you can download each file or click **Download all** to download every file that still exists. A card of more than six files shows the first four until you click **Show more**. When every file in a card is an image, the card shows the images together; click the list button to see their names and sizes. Images, text, and code files can also be previewed; other files, such as videos, PDFs, and archives, are download-only. Pontia reads the file from the device when you open or download it, so a file that was moved or deleted is no longer available.

When a Bot attaches files to a reply, they appear in the Bot chat as a card with each file's type and size. Images are shown inline and open full size when clicked; the viewer pages through the other images of the same card. Click a text or code file to preview it. Click the download button to save any file.

## Start a Bot chat

A new Bot greets you in your Dashboard language and waits for your first message. Once it understands what you want help with, it can fill in its description if it is empty. You can edit the description in Bot settings at any time. Clear it to let the Bot write a new one.

## Quote a Bot chat message

In a Bot chat, right-click a message, or click the **⋯** button that appears next to it when you hover over it, and choose **Reply**. For one attached file or image, choose **Quote file** or **Quote image** from the same menu. To quote part of a message, select it and choose **Quote** above the selection. On a phone, press and hold a message; the menu also offers **Copy** and **Select text**. Shift+right-click opens the browser's own menu.

The quote appears above the composer; click **×** to remove it. Quoting another message replaces it, and a message needs text to be sent with a quote. The Bot receives the full quoted text. Click a quote in a sent message to scroll back to the original, even when it is in older history.

## Chat commands

Type `/` in the composer to see commands available in the current context:

| Command | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `/new` | Start a new Session, keeping the current Workspace when possible |
| `/rename` | Rename the current Session |
| `/compact` | Summarize older context while the Session is idle, when supported |
| `/exit` | End Pontia's active control of the current Session |
| `/pin` | Pin or unpin the current Session |
| `/archive` | Archive or unarchive the current Session |

`/exit` ends Pontia's control of the Session. The Agent Client manages the lifecycle and storage of its native conversation.

## Keyboard shortcuts

Chat pages provide these shortcuts:

| Shortcut | Action |
| --- | --- |
| `Alt+J` / `Alt+K` | Move to the next or previous active chat |
| `Alt+1` … `Alt+9` | Open an active chat by sidebar position |
| `Alt+N` | Open New chat |
| `Alt+L` | Focus the composer |
| `Alt+M` | Switch to the next device. Add `Shift` to go back. |
| `Alt+C` / `Alt+W` | On New chat, switch to the next Agent Client or Workspace. Add `Shift` to go back. |
| `Alt+?` | Show the shortcut reference |
| `Ctrl+B` (`Cmd+B` on macOS) | Toggle the sidebar |

## Delete a Bot

Open the Bot's settings by clicking its name at the top of the chat, then choose **Delete Bot** at the bottom. On a phone, use **Delete Bot** in the top bar's **More** menu.

Deleting permanently removes the Bot, its chat history, and its directory under `$PONTIA_HOME/bot`. It cannot be undone. Memories, `USER.md`, and Workspaces are shared by all Bots and are kept, as is the history of the Bot's helper Sessions.

A Bot can be deleted only when it is not working and all of its helpers are closed. The confirmation lists any open helpers; ask the Bot to close them, or open each one and end it. You can delete the last Bot. Memory organization (dreaming) then pauses until you create a new Bot.

## Organize Sessions

Use a Session's action menu to rename, pin, archive, or end it. The **Sessions** page separates active, archived, and pinned Sessions. Archiving removes a Session from the active list without deleting its recorded control state.

The chat header also shows available metadata such as Workspace, Git branch and status, model, context usage, and Client. Fields appear only when the selected Client reports them.

For service or connection errors, continue with [Troubleshooting](/docs/troubleshooting).
